From 2a8f90ee70be5ed8de43ebea803ba74bec9a317d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: cam <cam@x.invalid>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 23:20:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: media: i2c: st,vd55g1: describe the VD55G0

The Surface Pro 11 infrared camera is an STMicroelectronics VD55G0, a
monochrome global shutter sensor with one CSI-2 D-PHY lane that the
vd55g1 schema already describes in every other respect: clock, the vcore,
vddio and vana supplies, the active low reset and the one-lane endpoint.

Add st,vd55g0 to the compatible list. The VD55G0 reports another model
identifier (0x3047 in the 16 bit register at offset 0 on this device,
against 0x53354731 and 0x53354733 for the others) and takes another
firmware patch, so vd55g1.c does not bind it: the node stays inert until
a driver exists. The address is not fixed to 0x10 on this board, which
uses 0x60.

Assisted-by: Claude Sonnet 5.5
---
 .../devicetree/bindings/media/i2c/st,vd55g1.yaml          | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/media/i2c/st,vd55g1.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/media/i2c/st,vd55g1.yaml
index 58b1f9e85..629541741 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/media/i2c/st,vd55g1.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/media/i2c/st,vd55g1.yaml
@@ -14,7 +14,8 @@ maintainers:
 description: |-
  The STMicroelectronics VD55G1 is a global shutter image sensor with an active
  array size of 804H x 704V. It is programmable through I2C interface. The I2C
- address is fixed to 0x10.
+ address of the VD55G1 and VD55G4 is fixed to 0x10; a board may use another
+ address for the VD55G0.
 
  Image data is sent through MIPI CSI-2, which is configured as only 1 data
  lane. The sensor provides 4 GPIOS that can be used for external LED signal
@@ -26,11 +27,14 @@ allOf:
 properties:
   compatible:
     enum:
+      - st,vd55g0
       - st,vd55g1
       - st,vd55g4
       - st,vd65g4
     description:
-      VD55G1 and VD55G4 are monochrome variants, while VD65G4 is a color one.
+      VD55G0, VD55G1 and VD55G4 are monochrome variants, while VD65G4 is a
+      color one. The VD55G0 has another model identifier and another firmware
+      patch than the others, so the vd55g1 driver does not bind it.
 
   reg:
     maxItems: 1
